5. ENGLISH METADATA CHECK (pasted_file broadened scope sentence)
================================================================================
Context now reads: "Fallback for non-image data URIs with no usable name, including invalid
percent encoding, whether or not a MIME type is present. Also used as synthetic upload
metadata; valid names and attachment bytes stay unchanged. A 100px tile caption may truncate;
maxCells is advisory, not measured fit."
Verified against the code (read, not executed):
- src/renderer/src/features/chat/utils/get-file-name.ts: image data URIs return
  ui.chat.composer_media.pasted_image; every other `data:` URI returns ...pasted_file in BOTH
  the nameMatch branch (decodeURIComponent throws) and the no-name branch — so a MIME-type-
  bearing URI without a name= still lands here, which is exactly the correction the old note
  ("has no name or MIME type") needed.
- src/renderer/src/features/chat/utils/attachment-encode.ts (~line 155): "Synthetic names for
  unnamed data URLs follow the active locale and become upload metadata. Valid decoded names
  stay verbatim; the original dataUrl (and therefore its bytes/MIME) is passed untouched."
  Matches "Also used as synthetic upload metadata; valid names and attachment bytes stay
  unchanged" word for word in substance.
The broadened sentence is accurate. No finding.

