6. LEDGER RECORDING — NOT PERFORMED BY ME, command and row handed to the manager
================================================================================
The writer is node scripts/i18n/ledger-assemble.mjs (i18n/ledger.json rows + a copy of the
receipt under i18n/receipts/<instance>.json). It WRITES two tracked files, and my brief
forbids editing any repository file, so I did not run it. I also did not run --dry-run on it
(no such documented mode) and I make no claim about its output.
Its receipt contract matches this receipt's shape: multi-namespace receipts put each namespace
under namespaces.<ns> with its own status, findings and role-labelled hashes; it reads
source_sha256/target_sha256 from that block; an explicit findings: [] is required (absent is
not zero); instance must be the real 12-hex run id and must equal --auditor-instance. The
per-namespace hashes in my receipt are the four-on-disk values, so the rows it derives should
land as status "audited" with result clean.
Per-namespace invocation the manager needs (one run each, same receipt, same instance):
  node scripts/i18n/ledger-assemble.mjs --locale hi \
    --file src/i18n/catalogues/hi/ui.chat.json \
    --auditor-instance 157203ee10c3 --auditor-model deepseek/deepseek-flash \
    --receipt <canonical i18n/receipts path> \
    --translator-agent i18n-translator --translator-model anthropic/claude-sonnet-5-5 \
    --scope "<scope line from this receipt>" --date 2026-11-10
  …repeating with ui.chat.composer_media.json and ui.common.actions.json.
Until those rows exist, ledger-check.mjs keeps failing for hi on the "stale / does not name the
English source bytes" assertions seen in §2.4 — expected at this head, for all locales.

